  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at the 9:30 Club in Washington, DC, on April 26, 2019, marking their first show following the release of their album In League With Dragons [1]. The setlist featured a mix of new material and deep cuts, including the album’s title track and “Done Bleeding,” which was the first archived performance of that song [1][5]. The band also played several rare tracks, such as “Duke Ellington” and “For The Krishnacore Bands,” both of which appeared in the archive for the first time during this show [1][5]. Additionally, the group revisited older songs like “Magpie” and “Passaic, 1975,” which had not been played in archived shows for over a decade [5]. The performance included spoken introductions for “Done Bleeding” and “No Children” [1]. The recommended recording, taped by LMGBTapes, is a matrix mix of soundboard and audience microphones that captures the full 106-minute set [1]. Listeners praised the audio quality, with one noting it feels like being at the front of the room, while another highlighted how well it captures the crowd atmosphere [2][4]. This recording is the only one available for this date and has received a five-star rating from three users [1][5].",
